Description: outline editor for book chapter notes
 Notterizmus is a GNOME outline editor for taking notes on book chapters.
 Items are numbered automatically (Ⅰ, Ⅰ.1, Ⅰ.1.a) with tree connectors, and
 the result is copied as formatted HTML that pastes cleanly into TopCoding.
 .
 It supports bullets for notes, pros and cons, bold and italic text, tables,
 Excalidraw drawings, structure-aware paste, document-wide undo, selection
 scopes, multiple cursors, find and replace, a chapter list, earlier versions
 of each chapter and spell checking.
